    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1143">

                <pb facs="0943" n="827" sameAs="frus:frus1912/pg827"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 812.00/4708b.</note>
                <head ana="#head_untitled-inferred-from-preceding-sibling-head">[Untitled]</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1912-08-21T15:00:00-05:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">August 21, 1912—3 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Department’s 907, of July 19. <hi rendition="#italic">Vicksburg</hi>, which
                    sailed from San Diego August 22, will proceed first to Guaymas, arriving there
                    about August 28, and later proceed to the other west-coast ports in her
                    itinerary. So inform Mexican Government.</p>
                <p>In view of the situation that has arisen in Sonora the <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Vicksburg</hi> has secret orders to remain at Guaymas for the protection of
                    American citizens and American interests in that region until it is possible to
                    foresee with more or less certainty what will be the course of events.</p>
                <p>The <hi rendition="#italic">Des Moines</hi> will make a casual visit to the
                    east-coast ports similar to that outlined for the west coast, and will start
                    some time <pb facs="0944" n="828" xml:id="pg828"/> during the first week in
                    September, going first to Tampico, and touching later at Vera Cruz and Progreso,
                    and possibly at Coatzacoalcos. You will be informed of itinerary later. Make
                    same representations to the Mexican Government for her as for <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Vicksburg.</hi>
                </p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Huntington Wilson.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
